Member Inner Class

Interview Questions

1. What is a member inner class?
-->A member inner class is a non-static class declared directly inside another class.
        
        It can access all members (including private members) of the outer class.
        
        Example:
        
        class Outer {
        
            class Inner {
                void show() {
                    System.out.println("Member Inner Class");
                }
            }
        
            public static void main(String[] args) {
                Outer o = new Outer();
                Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();
                i.show();
            }
        }
        
        Output:
        
        Member Inner Class





2. Can a member inner class have constructors?
-->Yes.
        
        A member inner class can have constructors like any normal class.
        
        Example:
        
        class Outer {
        
            class Inner {
                Inner() {
                    System.out.println("Constructor called");
                }
            }
        
            public static void main(String[] args) {
                Outer o = new Outer();
                Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();
            }
        }
        
        Output:
        
        Constructor called




3. How do you create an object of a member inner class?
-->First create the outer class object, then create the inner class object.

Syntax:

Outer obj = new Outer();
Outer.Inner in = obj.new Inner();

Example:

class Outer {

    class Inner {
        void show() {
            System.out.println("Hello");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Outer obj = new Outer();
        Outer.Inner in = obj.new Inner();
        in.show();
    }
}

Output:

Hello




4. Can a member inner class have private/protected access modifiers?
-->Yes.

      A member inner class can be:
      
      private
      protected
      public
      default
      
      Example:
      
      class Outer {
      
          private class A { }
      
          protected class B { }
      
          public class C { }
      
          class D { }
      }




5. Can we declare static methods inside a member inner class?
-->No.

A non-static member inner class cannot have static methods (except static final constants and, in modern Java, certain static members are allowed, but interview answer: No).

Invalid Example:

class Outer {

    class Inner {

        static void show() { // Compilation error
            System.out.println("Hello");
        }
    }
}




6. Can a member inner class extend a class and implement an interface?
-->Yes.

A member inner class can both extend a class and implement an interface.

Example:

class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal Sound");
    }
}

interface Test {
    void display();
}

class Outer {

    class Inner extends Animal implements Test {

        public void display() {
            System.out.println("Display Method");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Outer o = new Outer();
        Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();

        i.sound();
        i.display();
    }
}

Output:

Animal Sound
Display Method





Interview Tip
        Inner Class → A class inside another class or interface.
        Member Inner Class → A non-static inner class that belongs to an object of the outer class.
        Object creation: Outer.Inner obj = outerObject.new Inner();
        Access outer object: Outer.this
        Fully qualified name: Outer.Inner
        Can access private members of outer class: Yes.
